# Grazian et al. (2020, ApJ 897, 94), Table 2 (space density of z ~ 5.5 AGNs in CANDELS); checked against arXiv:2006.02451v1
# Sample: two spectroscopically confirmed AGNs (GDN3333, z = 5.186, M1450 = -22.56; GDS3073, z = 5.563, M1450 = -22.10)
#         in 551.5 arcmin^2 of CANDELS GOODS-N, GOODS-S and EGS
# Redshift: 5.0 < z < 6.1; z ~ 5.5
# Magnitude definition: M1450
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-6 cMpc^-3 (H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7). The paper computes Phi = N / V (2 objects over
#       the comoving volume of 5.0 < z < 6.1, 1/Vmax without any magnitude-bin division) and plots it with mag^-1 luminosity functions,
#       i.e. it is effectively per 1-mag bin.
# Note: Errors are Gehrels (1986) 1-sigma deltas for N = 2 (upper, lower), not limit values.
# Note: No incompleteness correction is applied, so the paper calls this a lower limit. The format has no lower-limit type, so it is
#       kept as a data row with this warning. If the (poorly searched) EGS area were excluded, Phi would increase by ~1.6.
#
# M1450  Phi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
 -22.330  1.291  1.717  0.854
